      "side": 1,
      "message": "How does this look as the API change for Curve 25519 support?\n\nSome things to highlight:\n\n- Requires support for TRUSTED_ENVIRONMENT, no support in STRONGBOX\n- Mandates a single purpose for keys, one of SIGN (Ed25519), ATTEST_KEY (Ed25519) or AGREE_KEY (X25519).  It seems to be theoretically possible to convert between Montgomery \u0026 twisted Edwards versions of the curve (https://blog.filippo.io/using-ed25519-keys-for-encryption/), but doesn\u0027t seem like a good idea in practice.\n- Mandates Digest::NONE for Ed25519 (as it internally digests)\n- Expects support for importing both PKCS#8 format keys (OIDs from https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/rfc8410#section-3) and raw format keys.",
      "revId": "a65f60be3c1e4c751f2a2397414bcbe61b206070",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
